  "summary": "Prompt injection attacks involve injecting malicious instructions or data into an LLM-Integrated Application's input to manipulate its output. Existing studies on defenses against these attacks often lack a principled and comprehensive evaluation approach. This limitation has resulted in a lack of systematic understanding, with current works primarily relying on case studies.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "statement": "Prompt injection attacks are designed to insert malicious instructions or data into an LLM-Integrated Application's input, causing it to generate outcomes desired by an attacker.",
